  "source_attribution": "The s 14 difference image follows the target-shaped pixel illumination, with a descriptive positive-deficit centroid offset 0.560 pixel. The target lies near a pixel boundary, so this scalar offset is not a calibrated source probability. All 25 Gaia sources within 60 arcsec were screened at the conservative minimum 58.485 ppt aperture loss; no non-target source is capable under optimistic G-band full-capture assumptions. The target-like deficit and the neighbor census support target attribution at this bounded review level.",
  "independent_reduction": "Independent custom TESScut extraction of the s 14 deeper event at BTJD 1705.35681 reproduces the loss: central 1 x 1,3 x 3,5 x 5 apertures give 63.759,61.550,58.485 ppt. QLP alternative aperture depths 61.576/70.331/73.799 ppt test additional dilution but are not another pipeline; the custom pixel reduction supplies the independent extraction check.",
  "limitations": "The sector 26 egress-only model is excluded from adopted timing and depth. Depths depend on aperture dilution. Pixel centroids and Gaia G-band capability proxies are descriptive rather than calibrated TESS PRF likelihoods. Timing fit errors exclude model/pipeline systematics. No exhaustive all-sector characterization or Monte Carlo was performed. Physical confirmation is separate from pending catalogue novelty.",
